  This is a starting point written by a software assistant, not by a
  lawyer. Before Legion is sold or given to anyone outside your own
  organisation, two things must happen:

    1. Every [BRACKETED] field below must be filled in with real
       values — you cannot license software as an entity that does
       not exist yet.
    2. A lawyer qualified in [JURISDICTION] must review the whole
       document. Limitation-of-liability and warranty-disclaimer
       clauses are exactly the clauses courts refuse to enforce when
       they are worded wrongly, and this is security software: the
       clauses that matter most are the ones about what happens when
       a breach is not detected.

  Delete this banner once both are done.

